  <string name="help_faq_audio_q">How do I play audio recitation?</string>
  <string name="help_faq_audio_a">Open any Quran page and tap once to reveal the floating Modern Audio Bar at the bottom. Tap the Reciter pill to choose between over 20+ authentic reciters. Tap the Play button to stream or listen gaplessly.</string>
  <string name="help_faq_reading_q">How do I view translations &amp; tafsir?</string>
  <string name="help_faq_reading_a">While reading, tap the Translation icon in the Top HUD or long-press an ayah and select Translation. You can download and prioritize 70+ translations in Settings > Translations.</string>
  <string name="help_faq_bookmark_q">How do I bookmark a page or ayah?</string>
  <string name="help_faq_bookmark_a">To bookmark a whole page, tap the Bookmark ribbon in the Top HUD. To bookmark a specific ayah, long-press the ayah and tap Bookmark or assign tags for easy organization.</string>
  <string name="help_faq_memorizer_q">How do I use Spaced-Repetition Memorization?</string>
  <string name="help_faq_memorizer_a">Long-press any ayah or select a surah and tap Memorize to enter the Intelligent Memorizer. The app helps you memorize ayah-by-ayah through progressive audio loops and recitation testing.</string>
  <string name="help_faq_display_q">How do I adjust Night Mode &amp; text size?</string>
  <string name="help_faq_display_a">Go to Settings > Appearance to toggle Night Mode. You can fine-tune both Text Brightness and Background Brightness sliders in real-time.</string>
  <string name="help_faq_nav_q">How do I jump quickly to any Surah or Juz?</string>
  <string name="help_faq_nav_a">Tap the Jump icon in the Top HUD or the bottom page scrubber. Select the Surah tab to pick a surah and ayah, or use the Page/Juz tab to jump straight to any part of the Quran.</string>
  <string name="help_faq_search_q">How do I search across the Quran?</string>
  <string name="help_faq_search_a">Tap the Search icon on the Home Hub or Reader HUD. You can search instantly by Arabic text, Surah names, or translated words across your downloaded translations.</string>

